<article class="env-lemma" id="04N9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04N9">Lemma <span data-tag="04N9">66.22.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $x \in |X|$ be a point. Let $d \in \{ 0, 1, 2, \ldots , \infty \} $. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the dimension of the local ring of $X$ at $x$ (Definition <a href="/tag/04NA" data-tag="04NA">66.10.2</a>) is $d$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}) = d$ for some geometric point $\overline{x}$ lying over $x$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}) = d$ for any geometric point $\overline{x}$ lying over $x$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The equivalence of (2) and (3) follows from the fact that the isomorphism type of $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ only depends on $x \in |X|$, see Remark <a href="/tag/04K4" data-tag="04K4">66.19.11</a>. Using Lemma <a href="/tag/04KF" data-tag="04KF">66.22.1</a> the equivalence of (1) and (2)$+$(3) comes down to the following statement: Given any local ring $R$ we have $\dim (R) = \dim (R^{sh})$. This is More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06LK" data-tag="06LK">15.46.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>